      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# 01 · Load Audio → Audio Timeline → one audio per speaker\n1. Pick a file in **Load Audio** and queue the workflow **once**: the connected audio then appears on the timeline of *Audio Timeline*.\n2. **Sections** = the parts you keep. Drag on the ruler to mark one (drag more to add), drag their edges to trim, drag the blocks in the *output* strip to reorder, ✂ Split at the playhead, Delete to remove.\n3. **Analyze speakers** (set *num_speakers* if you know it). Then fix the result like in an editor: drag a clip's edges to trim, drag a clip onto another speaker's lane to reassign it, drag in an empty lane to draw a clip, **+ Speaker** for a manual one, double-click a name to rename. **Undo/Redo** are there.\n4. The node gets one audio output per lane (`speaker_1`, `speaker_2`, …); connect what you need. Click a lane + **Play** to listen.\n\n*Speaker detection needs a one-time setup, see the README.*"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
